  "question": {
    "text": "Two satellites of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;revolve around the earth in circular orbits of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> respectively. The ratio of orbital speeds of the satellites respectively is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The orbital velocity is given&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></mfenced></msqrt></math></p><p>where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;is the mass of earth and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the orbit of satellite.</p><p>The velocity of the satellite with mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>and the velocity of the satellite with mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio of the velocities is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
